@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Medium BPMN process — service+user tasks, parallel & exclusive gateways, error boundary, 2 lanes.
'   usecase:      Order fulfillment with payment + shipping handoff.
'   complexity:   medium
'   domain:       business-process
' ============================================================================
title Example BPMN Process - Order Fulfillment

' Shape -> BPMN mapping (PlantUML has no native BPMN):
'   circle/usecase (thin) = start event
'   circle (thick/double) = end event
'   rectangle             = task (user/service/manual)
'   usecase diamond       = gateway
'   -->                    = sequence flow
'   ..>                    = message flow (dashed)
' Boundary events: drawn as a small concentric circle on a task.

' --- Lanes (single pool, two lanes) --------------------------------------
|Order Desk|
|Warehouse|

' --- Start ----------------------------------------------------------------
usecase " " as Start

' --- Tasks ----------------------------------------------------------------
rectangle "Receive Order" as T1
rectangle "Charge Payment" as T2
rectangle "Pack Items" as T3
rectangle "Ship Order" as T4
rectangle "Refund Customer" as T5

' --- Gateways -------------------------------------------------------------
usecase "Split (AND)" as And1
usecase "Paid?" as Xor1

' --- End ------------------------------------------------------------------
usecase " " as EndOk
usecase " " as EndFail

Start --> T1
T1 --> And1
' Parallel gateway splits into two concurrent branches
And1 --> T2
And1 --> T3

' Error boundary on payment — if charge fails, branch to refund
T2 --> Xor1
Xor1 --> T4 : (yes)
Xor1 --> T5 : (no — payment error)

' Boundary event annotation for the error attached to T2
note right of T2
  <b>Error boundary event</b>
  (concentric circle on task)
  If payment raises an error,
  the token jumps to the
  compensation path (Refund).
end note

T3 --> T4
T4 --> EndOk
T5 --> EndFail

note top of And1
  <b>Parallel gateway (AND)</b>
  Forks into concurrent branches;
  the matching join waits for all.
end note

note right of Xor1
  <b>Exclusive gateway (XOR)</b>
  One path taken based on condition.
end note

note bottom of EndOk
  <b>End event (thick circle)</b>
end note

@enduml
